<title>USA: CORUS Bankshares Inc Q4 net rises.</title>
<headline>CORUS Bankshares Inc Q4 net rises.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-01-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>1996			1995</p>
<p> Shr			$  0.72		   $ 0.66</p>
<p> Net			 10,776		   10,031</p>
<p> Avg shrs		  14,996		   15,145</p>
<p>	  12 MONTHS</p>
<p> Shr			$  2.93		   $ 2.35</p>
<p> Net			 43,905		   35,770</p>
<p> Avg shrs		  14,994		   15,241</p>
<p>(All data above 000s except per share numbers)  </p>
<p>NOTE: 1996 Q4 results include a charge-off of $4 million in student loans related to an agreement with U.S. Department of Education as part of the government's ongoing investigation into the company's student loan servicing operations.</p>
<p>1996 Q4 provision for possible loan losses totaled $4 million vs $2.8 million in 1995 Q4.</p>
<p>1996 year provision for possible loan losses totaled $16 million vs $5.8 million in 1995.</p>
<p>Assets $2.22 billion vs $2.13 billion</p>
<p>Loans $1.59 billion vs $1.53 billion</p>
<p>Deposits $1.90 billion vs $1.90 billion</p>
<p>		((Chicago newsdesk 312 408 8787))</p>
</text>
